course: dictionary
lesson: 10307
title: Tow: pulling and following
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tow is a word with three meanings. To tow something is to pull it along behind a vehicle or boat, using a rope, chain or bar. A tow is the act of towing, as in «give someone a tow». The third meaning is «in tow», which means following closely behind.
explain: Use context to find the meaning. «A breakdown truck will tow the broken-down car to the garage.» The clues are broken-down and garage: the car cannot drive, so something must pull it. Try your meaning in the sentence: «A breakdown truck will pull the broken-down car to the garage.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Watch for «in tow». «The little boy walked into the shop with his three sisters in tow.» Nobody is pulling anyone on a rope here. The sisters are following closely behind him. The words around the phrase tell you what it means, not the single word tow.
explain: Tow can also describe a pulling force that is not a person. «A glider has no engine, so it is towed up into the air» by another aircraft. The tow pulls the glider along, and then the glider can float on rising warm air.
fact: To tow means to pull something behind a vehicle or boat, using a rope, chain or bar.
fact: A tow is the act of towing: «give someone a tow».
fact: «In tow» means following closely behind: «with three children in tow».
fact: A «tow truck» pulls broken-down cars, and a «tow-rope» is the rope used for pulling.
fact: «A car parked illegally can be towed away.» This means it can be pulled away by a tow truck.
exercise: «The breakdown truck will tow the broken-down car to the garage.» What does tow mean here? | *To pull behind using a rope or chain | To park it in a quiet street | To paint it a new colour | To push it up a hill with your hands
exercise: «The children walked to school with three friends in tow.» What does in tow mean? | Waiting at the school gate | Carrying heavy bags | Fighting over sweets | *Following closely behind
exercise: «Dad gave me a tow after my bike broke down.» In this sentence, what is a tow? | A broken part of a bike | A type of bike | *The act of pulling something to help it | A rude word
test: «A glider has no engine, so it is towed up into the air.» What does towed mean here? | Flown with its own engine | Pushed off a cliff by the wind | *Pulled along behind an aircraft | Painted bright red
test: «A car parked illegally can be towed away.» What can happen to the car? | It can be painted by the police | It can be sold to a shop | It can be driven away by its owner | *It can be pulled away by a tow truck
exam: «Electric cars can be hard to charge on long trips or when towing.» What does towing mean here? | *Pulling something behind the car | Parking in a small space | Driving very fast on the motorway | Charging the battery from the sun
